<title>AUSTRALIA: Qantas Australian Defence contract extended.</title>
<headline>Qantas Australian Defence contract extended.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Qantas Airways Ltd said on Tuesday it had been awarded a 12 month extension of its contract to provide both domestic and international travel the Australian Department of Defence.</p>
<p>Qantas chief executive James Strong said in a statement the Department of Defence had exercised its option for the extension of the original contract, worth about A$75 million a year, which the airline won in 1995.</p>
<p>The new agreement is effective from May 8, 1998 to May 7, 1999.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
